NOTE: This is a Vortex extension, NOT a mod. It lets the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/vortex]Vortex[/url] mod manager manage [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/games/survivallog/mods]Survival Log mods[/url].

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Finds the game.[/b] Vortex finds a Steam install of Survival Log by itself. You can also set the game folder by hand.[/*]
[*][b]Installs BepInEx.[/b] When the game folder has no BepInEx, Vortex downloads the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx Pack for Survival Log[/url] and installs it as a mod, with no extra step.[/*]
[*][b]Keeps your own BepInEx.[/b] If you already installed BepInEx by hand, Vortex does not download the pack and does not change your BepInEx files. It installs only the mods. The Health Check of Vortex can then say that a mod misses the BepInEx pack: your mods still work, so hide the warning or let Vortex install the pack.[/*]
[*][b]Installs mods into the right folder.[/b] Mods go into [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font]. When you remove a mod in Vortex, only its files leave the game folder.[/*]
[*][b]Opens the game's folders.[/b] The folder menu of the Mods page opens the mods folder ([font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font]), the mods config folder, the BepInEx log, the Unity log, the saves folder, the Steam store page, and the wiki.[/*]
[*][b]Knows the game version.[/b] Vortex shows the game version, for example 1.1.19131, and tells you when a game update arrives.[/*]
[/list]
Tested with Vortex 2.9.0 and Survival Log 1.1.19131.

[b]This is unofficial.[/b] Neither Nexus Mods nor the developer of Survival Log makes, supports, or endorses this extension. The BepInEx team does not endorse it either.

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/vortex]Vortex[/url] if you do not have it.[/*]
[*]In Vortex, open [b]Games[/b], search for [b]Survival Log[/b], and click [b]Manual add[/b] on its card. Vortex installs this extension. You can also click [b]Mod manager download[/b] in the Files tab of this page.[/*]
[*]Restart Vortex when it asks. If Survival Log is not under your managed games yet, click [b]Add game[/b] on its card.[/*]
[*]Wait a moment. Vortex downloads the BepInEx pack, and [b]BepInEx Pack for Survival Log[/b] shows as Enabled in your mod list.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Add mods[/b][/size]
On a Survival Log mod page, click [b]Mod manager download[/b] (or [b]Vortex[/b] at the top of the page). Vortex downloads the mod, installs it, and deploys it. For a zip that you downloaded yourself, drop it onto the [b]Drop File(s)[/b] area of the [b]Mods[/b] page in Vortex.

The first start with a new BepInEx takes longer than normal, needs an internet connection, and opens a console window: do not close it, because that also closes the game. Details are on the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx pack page[/url].

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
In Vortex, open [b]Extensions[/b] and remove [b]Game: Survival Log[/b]. Your mods stay in the game folder, and when you install the extension again, Vortex shows the same mod list.

[size=4][b]Source and license[/b][/size]
